{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tightlip is a SwiftPM build-tool plugin. The plugin attaches to a target, reads a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Secrets.yml","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" config at the target’s source root, resolves declared environment variables, and emits a Swift source file containing a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Secrets","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" enum compiled into your binary.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Installation","anchor":"Installation"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Swift Package Manager","anchor":"Swift-Package-Manager"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the package as a dependency:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Package.swift",".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/Tightlip\", from: \"1.0.0\"),"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Attach the plugin to a target:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    plugins: [.plugin(name: \"Lipservice\", package: \"Tightlip\")]",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drop "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Secrets.yml"},{"type":"text","text":" at the target’s source root, e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/MyApp\/Secrets.yml"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Xcode project","anchor":"Xcode-project"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"File → Add Package Dependencies…"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" → paste ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/Tightlip"},{"text":" → set Dependency Rule to ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Up to Next Major","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1.0.0"},{"text":". (","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add Local…","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" also works for vendored checkouts.)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the target’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build Phases → Run Build Tool Plug-ins"}]},{"type":"text","text":", add "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lipservice"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create "},{"code":"<TargetName>\/Secrets.yml","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at the project root (the directory containing "},{"code":".xcodeproj","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). "},{"code":"<TargetName>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the target’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"display name"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; the plugin resolves the path on the filesystem, not through Xcode’s group tree, so the file’s position in the Project Navigator is irrelevant. For a stock app template this is the "},{"code":"<TargetName>\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" folder already at the top of the project."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference the generated enum anywhere in the target: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Secrets.revenueCatAPIKey"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Your-First-Secret","text":"Your First Secret","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create "},{"code":"Secrets.yml","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["# Secrets.yml","revenueCatAPIKey: REVENUECAT_API_KEY"],"syntax":"yaml","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The left side is the Swift property name; the right side names an environment variable Tightlip resolves at build time. Export the variable before building:"}]},{"code":["export REVENUECAT_API_KEY=\"appl_…\"","swift build"],"syntax":"bash","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference the generated enum in your code:"}]},{"code":["let client = RevenueCat(apiKey: Secrets.revenueCatAPIKey)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If ","type":"text"},{"code":"REVENUECAT_API_KEY","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is unset, the build fails with a clear error pointing at the missing variable. Every declared secret is required.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"What Just Happened","anchor":"What-Just-Happened","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At build time Tightlip:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parsed "},{"code":"Secrets.yml","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sourced "},{"code":"~\/.zshenv","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a clean zsh subshell and merged the result with "},{"code":"ProcessInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Resolved each declared env var to its current value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Emitted a Swift file containing a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Secrets"},{"type":"text","text":" enum, with each value XOR-encoded against a salt derived from the values themselves."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The compiler included that file in your target.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The XOR encoding defends against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"strings"},{"type":"text","text":"-style extraction from the shipped binary; see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/Obfuscation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the threat model."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the plugin to a target, drop in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Secrets.yml"},{"type":"text","text":", and start reading secrets at compile time."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/SectionedConfigs","doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/ConfigGrammar","doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSourcing"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/gettingstarted"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started with Tightlip","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Tightlip"}]},"references":{"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/ConfigGrammar":{"title":"Config Grammar","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/configgrammar","abstract":[{"text":"The accepted shape of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Secrets.yml","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", line by line.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/ConfigGrammar"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/Obfuscation":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/Obfuscation","role":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/obfuscation","title":"Obfuscation and Threat Model","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What the XOR encoding actually protects against, and what it doesn’t."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore":{"title":"Tightlip","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"A SwiftPM build-tool plugin that generates a typed Swift ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Secrets"},{"text":" enum from environment variables at build time.","type":"text"}]},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/EnvironmentSourcing":{"title":"How Environment Sourcing Works","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSourcing","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/environmentsourcing","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why your env vars resolve the same way whether you build from Xcode, the terminal, or CI."}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/SectionedConfigs":{"title":"Multi-Environment Configs","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/SectionedConfigs","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare staging and production secrets in one file and select between them per build."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/sectionedconfigs","type":"topic"}}}